{
  "name": "343. Batch create refusals carry error_type: caller_unsupported_parameter for a field the vendor's batch cannot take (batch error type)",
  "description": "Contract C4 agreement three and C6 (TXE-6972): a batch create the gateway refuses before anything is sent carries extra_fields.error_type, so a client classifies it by one field. A well-formed field the vendor's batch cannot take (a url a generateContent batch cannot run, an Imagen model on an image line, a line naming another model, a second url in one batch, Vertex metadata that cannot be a job label) is caller_unsupported_parameter with the field in error.param. A malformed batch or line (no model, no body) is caller_invalid_request. Every case is answered by the gateway alone: no vendor call is made, so the cases need no vendor quota. Folder 301 asserts the same field on its own refusal rows.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "[EXPECT-400] gemini batch error type: a second url in one batch is caller_unsupported_parameter naming the line",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"an image line beside a chat line is a 400 caller_unsupported_parameter naming requests[1].url\", function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql(400);",
              "  var j = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect((j.extra_fields || {}).error_type, pm.response.text()).to.eql('caller_unsupported_parameter');",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('x-bifrost-error-type'), 'the header carries the same value').to.eql('caller_unsupported_parameter');",
              "  pm.expect((j.error || {}).param, pm.response.text()).to.eql(\"requests[1].url\");",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.include(\"a batch runs one url\");",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"model\": \"gemini/gemini-2.5-flash-image\",\n  \"requests\": [\n    {\n      \"custom_id\": \"bet-url-1\",\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"url\": \"/v1/chat/completions\",\n      \"body\": {\n        \"model\": \"gemini-2.5-flash-image\",\n        \"messages\": [\n          {\n            \"role\": \"user\",\n            \"content\": \"Reply with the single word: ok\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"max_tokens\": 8\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"custom_id\": \"bet-url-2\",\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"url\": \"/v1/images/generations\",\n      \"body\": {\n        \"model\": \"gemini-2.5-flash-image\",\n        \"prompt\": \"A lighthouse at dusk\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/batches",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "batches"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
